-- lib/meaning.cub — meaning computed from the record (docs/language-derived-from-the-record.cub, §§2–4),
-- at the level of characters, with nothing added. The record is everything the store holds, every
-- text of every piece, as it is, and every turn said since. An occurrence is an event of the record;
-- the only identification is equality of characters. The present context is the turn; a past
-- occurrence is selected exactly when its context is identified with the present one, and the most
-- context identified is the longest end of the turn the record holds (context resolves by shrinking
-- the fiber, never by weighting). The meaning is the family of what followed the selected occurrences,
-- each to the end of its line, equal continuations being one: where they all agree the meaning is
-- determinate and is printed once; where they part, the family is printed as it is, every branch.
-- Used by `hyperactive chat` (lib/chat.cub) and by the server's /chat, which holds it in its running
-- process.
import "host.cub"

